    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 3c694a93485d9ddfea30d3f76e14b702fecab5b6 -->\n**Review (M3, safety tier): clean. It keeps `conflicts` until the merge-time refresh.**\n\n**What looks good**\n- **It builds on #1265 without duplicating it.** `declared_serves` is read inside the same `serves()` check, and shipped posts are still judged by their registry name.\n- **A bad `serves` is a clean error.** An empty list or an unknown kind word is refused, and the refusal says how to declare the kinds.\n- **A user plasma script that states nothing is now refused on a plasma table.** That is the safe direction, and a test pins it.\n- **Nothing risky added:** no new unwrap or panic, and no `.cps` or golden changes. The decision file is present.\n\n**Local results** (merged with main 13c4e75b, with the conflicts resolved locally):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: 1122 passed. That includes `post_serves_kind` 6, `post_serves_plasma` 1, `plasma_post`, `plasma_post_refusals`, `lathe_post` and `posting`.\n- `serves_is_read_from_the_manifest`: passes. Clippy is clean.\n- **Mutation checks:** each of these makes a pinning test fail:\n  - ignoring the declared kinds;\n  - accepting undeclared plasma;\n  - a `contains` that always returns true;\n  - dropping the declare hint;\n  - dropping the empty-`serves` error (caught by the dialect unit test).\n\n**Merge-time refresh** (the hunks touch logic, but both sides combine):\n- **`posting_serves.rs`:** keep both doc blocks and both `use` lines. Main's d1fec88a `unturned()` check still applies to a script that declares `serves`, so the turned-section refusal is not bypassed.\n- **`tests/post_serves_kind.rs`:** keep both sides' new tests.\n- After the refresh, re-run `post_serves_kind` and `lathe_post`.\n\n**Notes**\n1. **Behaviour change:** a user plasma script that states nothing now has to add `serves = [\"plasma\"];`. Worth a line in the release notes.\n2. **A malformed `serves` falls back silently.** `Script::words_global` (`crates/post/src/post/js.rs`) reads a `serves` that is neither a string nor an array (e.g. `serves = 5`) as \"states none\", so the dialect guess applies. That is the same as main today, but refusing it would be safer. Add a test pin with it.\n3. **One combination is unpinned:** a declared `serves = [\"mill-turn\"]` together with main's turned-section refusal.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
